--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Reference data
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

data/reference/tag_map.csv is derived in part from the Codifier of
Administrative-Territorial Units and Territories of Territorial Communities
(KATOTTG / КАТОТТГ), published by the Ministry of Development of Communities and
Territories of Ukraine on the Ukrainian open data portal:

  https://data.gov.ua/dataset/43c2a113-a032-4c8a-a409-3b5e1660bb38

Published under Creative Commons Attribution. Reuse is permitted, including
commercially, on condition that the source is cited, which this notice does.

The file also contains counts measured from the public Telegram channel
t.me/s/air_alert_ua, and a status and note column recording where the two
vocabularies disagree. Those columns are this project's own work.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/reference/poland_outline.json
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Poland feature of ne_10m_admin_0_countries, extracted unmodified from
Natural Earth:

  https://github.com/nvkelso/natural-earth-vector

Natural Earth is in the public domain. Its terms ask that no one claim exclusive
rights over the data and impose no attribution obligation; this notice records
the source because a measurement without a stated source is an assertion.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/reference/border_km.csv
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Generated by tools/border_distance.py. The distances are this project's own
computation, but two of the three inputs are not.

The centre point and area of each administrative unit come from ua-geo:

  https://github.com/alexbabintsev/ua-geo

which is MIT licensed and joins the Ukrainian KATOTTG register to boundary
relations in OpenStreetMap. The centre points are therefore derived from
OpenStreetMap data, which is licensed under the Open Database License (ODbL).
Anyone redistributing this column, or a product derived from it, should treat it
as a derivative database: attribute OpenStreetMap contributors, and share any
altered version of the column under the same licence.

  https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

This project's contribution to the file is the distance computation and the
interval, and those are covered by the licence in LICENSE. The dependency on
ODbL data is stated here rather than buried, because it constrains what a
downstream consumer may do and that is not the kind of thing to discover later.
